Q1) Define Denial of Service (DoS) attack and explain its working
principles along with SYN flood and HTTP flood attack types.

DoS Attack:
A Denial of Service (DoS) attack is a cyber attack in which an
attacker sends a large amount of traffic or requests to a system
to make it unavailable to normal users.

Working Principle:
1. Attacker sends many requests to the target.
2. The target tries to process the requests.
3. System resources become busy.
4. Normal users cannot access the service properly.

SYN Flood:
- The attacker sends many SYN requests.
- The server waits for connections that are not completed.
- This consumes server resources.

HTTP Flood:
- The attacker sends many HTTP requests to a web server.
- The server becomes overloaded.
- Normal users may face slow or unavailable service.


Q2) Python Program to Implement Caesar Cipher for Encryption
and Decryption. [20 Marks]
'''

text = input("Enter text: ")
shift = int(input("Enter shift value: "))

encrypted = ""

for ch in text:
    if ch.isupper():
        encrypted += chr((ord(ch) - ord('A') + shift) % 26 + ord('A'))
    elif ch.islower():
        encrypted += chr((ord(ch) - ord('a') + shift) % 26 + ord('a'))
    else:
        encrypted += ch

decrypted = ""

for ch in encrypted:
    if ch.isupper():
        decrypted += chr((ord(ch) - ord('A') - shift) % 26 + ord('A'))
    elif ch.islower():
        decrypted += chr((ord(ch) - ord('a') - shift) % 26 + ord('a'))
    else:
        decrypted += ch

print("Encrypted text:", encrypted)
print("Decrypted text:", decrypted)

